<speak>We definitely had different ideas. My daughter wanted photographs, my wife wanted to browse a small bookshop, and I wanted somewhere to sit without checking the time. In the end we managed all of that in one neighbourhood. The best part wasn't something we had booked. We found a little café, stayed longer than intended, and talked about ordinary things. I realised we hadn't done that for ages. At home, our conversations are often about who needs to be where, rather than anything we actually feel like discussing.</speak>